course: dictionary
lesson: 4077
title: Germanic
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Germanic is an adjective, and it usually starts with a capital G. It describes a family of languages, like a big family of cousins. English, German, Dutch, Swedish, Danish, Norwegian and Icelandic are all Germanic languages.
explain: «English is a Germanic language, a cousin of German, Dutch and Frisian.» This is why house is «Haus» in German and «huis» in Dutch. The words look alike because the languages share a family.
explain: Germanic can also describe ancient peoples of northern Europe, such as the Angles, Saxons, Goths and Vikings. The Anglo-Saxons were Germanic peoples who came to Britain and brought Old English with them.
explain: Use the clues around the word. If the sentence is about languages, words or cousins, Germanic means the language family. If it is about history, tribes or old peoples, it means those peoples and their cultures.
fact: Germanic is an adjective, and it usually has a capital G.
fact: «Germanic languages» are the family that includes English, German, Dutch and Swedish.
fact: «Germanic tribes» were ancient peoples of northern Europe, such as the Angles, Saxons, Goths and Vikings.
fact: Many everyday words have Germanic roots, such as house, mother, water and eat, while many long words come from Latin or French.
fact: Wednesday comes from «Woden's day», after the old Germanic god Woden, the same god the Norse called Odin.
exercise: «English is a Germanic language.» What does Germanic describe here? | A king who ruled Rome | *A family of languages that includes English and German | A kind of weather that is cold and wet | A type of food from Germany
exercise: Ella notices that house and «Haus» look alike. Why? | Because they were invented last week | *They come from the same Germanic family of languages | Because Haus is a German word for water | Because both words start with a capital letter
exercise: Which of these was a Germanic people? | Aztecs | Ancient Egyptians | Romans | *Saxons
test: «The Anglo-Saxons were Germanic peoples who came to Britain.» What does Germanic describe here? | A family of languages | A type of bread | *Ancient peoples of northern Europe | A modern train service
test: Which language is NOT in the Germanic family? | Dutch | *French | German | Swedish
exam: Which sentence uses Germanic to mean typical of Germany or German people? | *Her grandma baked a Germanic cake with apples and cinnamon | Germanic tribes lived in northern Europe long ago | English is a Germanic language | Wednesday comes from Woden's day
